; An inner program for the singleton wrapper: one key owns the state.
;
; The wrapper runs this program over its truths consed onto the inner
; solution, so the environment is (OWNER_KEY TRUTHS . ARGS) once
; OWNER_KEY is curried. The owner signs the next inner program's
; hash, the next coin's amount, and the extra conditions, bound to
; the singleton coin's own outpoint, so an authorization fits exactly
; one spend of exactly one coin. The odd-amount CREATE_OUTPUT is the
; wrapper's child marker, rewritten by the wrapper into the next
; singleton coin and its state output. NEXT_AMOUNT of -113 ends the
; lineage. EXTRA_CONDITIONS pass through the wrapper unchanged and
; must therefore create only even-amount outputs.
(program (OWNER_KEY (LAUNCHER MY_OUTPOINT MY_SPK MY_AMOUNT MY_INNER_HASH)
          NEXT_INNER_HASH NEXT_AMOUNT EXTRA_CONDITIONS SIG)
  (c (list ASSERT_SIG_MY_OUTPOINT OWNER_KEY
           (sha256tree (list NEXT_INNER_HASH NEXT_AMOUNT EXTRA_CONDITIONS))
           SIG)
  (c (list CREATE_OUTPUT NEXT_INNER_HASH NEXT_AMOUNT)
     EXTRA_CONDITIONS)))
